    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0708" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg610"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/1609: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-26T19:00:00+08:00">February 26, 1932—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 26—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My February 23, 3 p.m.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d675-f1"/> I have received a letter
                    from T. V. Soong from which I quote the following: <pb facs="0709" n="611"
                        xml:id="pg611"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I wonder if you have heard anything in the meanwhile from your
                            Government …<anchor n="68" xml:id="d675-f2"/> as payment for this month
                            will be due tomorrow.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
